{"name":"Misty Afternoon","hex":"#c6dcc7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"misty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered in mist; foggy.","Dim; vague; obscure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misty"},{"term":"afternoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the day from noon or lunchtime until sunset, evening, or suppertime or 6pm.","The later part of anything, often with implications of decline."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the afternoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Afternoon is the period from noon to sunset or evening. It is the time when the sun is descending from its peak in the sky to somewhat before its terminus at the horizon in the west. In human life, it occupies roughly the latter half of the standard work and school day. In literal terms, it refers to a time specifically after noon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/330px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afternoon","wikidata":"Q283102"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/1280px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropo